{
  "_provenance": [
    "Float reference parameters for the procedural 16-wedge connectome (connectome.build_procedural).",
    "Tuned 2026-09-19 in a Claude Code session. The brief's starting point saturated every population: with syn_decay 0.8 one spike delivers ~5*w of charge against a threshold of 1.",
    "Path: random search, then evolutionary refinement (scratch tooling, not in the repo), found a slow-synapse regime with one persistent bump. T3 uses push-pull drive (+d PEN_L, -d PEN_R), per the user's decision: PEN_L-only drive above the PEN threshold current turns the bump clockwise (see tests.t3_phases). The final step was a search scored on robustness: nominal plus 10 one-at-a-time +/-10% weight perturbations, 5 seeds, T1-T8. The result was rounded to 4 significant figures and re-verified with tune.py --robustness.",
    "Robustness: the one-at-a-time +/-10% gate (user decision) passes 10/10 on 5 seeds, and 5/10 fail at +/-15%. All-at-once corners at +/-10% pass 12/32 (recorded, not gated); every corner with w_ep and w_pe both -10% loses the bump. The result uses the smoothed metrics.bump_count the user adopted: with the unsmoothed metric and earlier T3 levels, one config (w_pe -10%) failed T5 on a single tick of rotation jitter. T3 levels were then raised to [0.5, 0.9, 1.3] x threshold current, because 0.3x sat on the dead-zone edge (history-dependent, ~0 rotation after a long hold). Pass/fail near the edge is chaotic: rounding the weights to 4 significant figures alone flipped one config.",
    "Units: 1 tick = dt ms; currents in the model's units, where the threshold current is v_thresh/tau."
  ],
